  "gradeRuleDescribe": {
    "yms_year": 114.0,
    "yms_smester": 1.0,
    "cls_id": "CE08320",
    "sub_id": "76180",
    "scr_dup": "001",
    "tpa_score_new": "Literature Review (30%)、Presentation (30%) 、Discussion (40%)",
    "tpa_score_new_en": "<div>Literature Review (30%)、Presentation (30%) 、Discussion (40%)</div>\n",
    "course_pol": "課堂上的行為始終應要及時、要專業、要做好準備、要有禮貌。同學、教師或其他講師間，應保有彼此尊嚴和相互尊重，才能進行有效的學習。為了確保有利於學習環境，冀望每個人都能做到以下幾點，彼此遵守課堂行為規則，習慣禮貌的文化。\n1.學生應準時出席上課。如果您的上課時間，無法按時到課，請不要選課。 除非您生病或有緊急情況，否則應在上課前，要準時到達教室，並坐在位子上。如果您有某種原因必須提早下課，請提前告知我。\n2.所有學生在課堂上都應尊重每個人，並且在任何時候都應以合理、負責和禮貌的態度行事。\n3.上課時請勿講話、閱讀、睡覺或做其他非本課程相關作業，除分組進行討論外，否則應盡量減少邊際對話。如果您正坐在一個可能在上課時和您聊天的人旁邊，請移到另一個座位，以免您屈服於誘惑。\n4.當同學簡報或提問時，您應該專心地聆聽。當您簡報時，您應該面對自己的小組或全班同學大聲說話，讓同學能聽清楚。\n5.允許使用筆記型電腦或平板等載具，進行課堂記筆記，否則應將其收起。\n6.要確保在上課時，關閉手機、PDA等移動設備，並收起及保持靜音。\n7.不得戴耳機上課。\n8.穿著整潔，不要暴露。",
    "course_pol_en": "Expected classroom behavior\nBehavior in the classroom should always be prompt, professional, prepared, and courteous. Effective learning can only be achieved by maintaining mutual dignity and mutual respect among classmates, teachers or other lecturers. In order to ensure a conducive learning environment, everyone is expected to do the following, abide by each other's classroom behavior rules, and get used to a culture of politeness.\n\n1. Students should attend class on time. If you cannot arrive at the class on time due to your class time, please do not register for the class. Unless you are sick or there is an emergency, you should be in your classroom on time and in your seat before class starts. If you have to leave class early for any reason, please let me know in advance.\n2. All students are expected to treat everyone with respect in the classroom and to behave reasonably, responsibly, and courteously at all times.\n3. Do not talk, read, sleep or do other non-course-related homework during class, except for group discussions, otherwise marginal conversations should be minimized. If you are sitting next to someone who might be chatting with you during class, move to another seat so you don't give in to temptation.\n4. You should listen attentively when classmates present or ask questions. When you present, you should speak loudly to your group or class so that they can hear you clearly.\n5. Laptops or tablets are allowed to take notes in class, otherwise they should be put away.\n6. Make sure that mobile devices such as mobile phones and PDAs are turned off during class, and put away and keep silent.\n7. Students are not allowed to wear earphones in class.\n8. Dress neatly without revealing.",
    "course_rem": null,
    "course_rem_en": null,
    "ais_meno": "<div>學習必須以誠信為基礎，任何學生企圖將自己未製作的作品，作為自己的作品，此行為是為不誠實行為。在作業、測驗或考試中作弊或抄襲的學生或協助他人的行為，該次成績以零分計，若是累犯，將依逢甲大學學生獎懲辦法提送。\n<ul>\n\t<li>考核時如果您抄襲他人的答案、或交作業時您交出全部或部分由他人撰寫的論文或作業，則被視為作弊。</li>\n\t<li>考核時如果您抄襲他人的答案、或交作業時您交出全部或部分由他人撰寫的論文或作業，則被視為作弊。</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n",
    "ais_meno_en": "<div>Learning must be based on honesty. Any student who attempts to use a work that he has not produced as his own is considered dishonest. Students who cheat or plagiarize in homework, tests or exams, or assist others, will be scored as zero. If they are repeat offenders, they will be submitted in accordance with the rewards and punishments for students of Feng Chia University.\n<ul>\n\t<li>It is considered cheating if you copy someone else&#39;s answers during an assessment, or if you turn in a paper or assignment that was written in whole or in part by someone else when you turned in an assignment.</li>\n\t<li>It is considered cheating if you copy someone else&#39;s answers during an assessment, or if you turn in a paper or assignment that was written in whole or in part by someone else when you turned in an assignment.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n",
    "ilearn_mk": "N"
  },
